        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks unite exquisite atomic control with a striking advance in precision measurement and tests of fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye are the clear central figures for the lattice-clock concept and its experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "Independent clock programs have achieved extraordinary performance and established wide scientific use.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The eventual prize framing may need to encompass a wider lineage of optical-clock development."
        ]
      }
    },
